        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] upsert_document.py** - Upserts a JSON document by its primary identifier using AWS DynamoDB.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] fetch_document.py** - Fetches a document by identifier from AWS DynamoDB.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] query_documents.py** - Queries documents by a field value or partition-style key in AWS DynamoDB.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] conditional_update.py** - Applies a conditional or version-aware update to one stored document in AWS DynamoDB.\n5. **[HELPER] database_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for AWS DynamoDB and AWS S3.\n6. **[HELPER] database_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for AWS DynamoDB.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] record_summary.py** - Summarizes retrieved document records.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] record_text_safety.py** - Checks user-generated document fields for unsafe content.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] record_translate.py** - Translates user-facing document fields using AWS Translate.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] record_export_archive.py** - Archives exported document snapshots or attachments in AWS S3.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
